      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historically, New Church’s economy has relied on farming, fishing, and oyster harvesting, staples of the Eastern Shore’s rural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/new-church-119740",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community’s name simply points to a newly built church at the time of its founding, a straightforward English place name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/new-church-119740",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Visitors can drop by the Virginia Welcome Center at New Church for maps, lodging tips, and local history during its open hours.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
